Value Required INTERFACE (\S+)
Value INSTANCE (\S+)
Value VRF (\S+)
Value AREA (\S+)
Value NETWORK_TYPE (\S+)
Value COST (\d+)
Value STATE (\S.*?)
Value DR (\S+)
Value BDR (\S+)
Value PASSIVE (Passive Interface)
Value AUTH (\S.*[Aa]uthentication)

# One record per interface in OSPF (feature 011, research R1). Timers, transmit delay, priority,
# speed, the neighbour count, traffic engineering and TI-LFA are not captured (FR-007). The DR and
# BDR lines name router IDs, not addresses (research R5). EOS prints md5 and sha keys alike, so
# AUTH stops before ", using key id" (research R6).
Start
  ^\S -> Continue.Record
  ^${INTERFACE} is \S+
  ^\s+Interface Address \S+, instance ${INSTANCE}, VRF ${VRF}, Area ${AREA}$$
  ^\s+Network Type ${NETWORK_TYPE}, Cost: ${COST}$$
  ^\s+Transmit Delay is \d+ sec, State ${STATE}(, Priority \d+)?$$
  ^\s+Designated Router is ${DR}$$
  ^\s+Backup Designated Router is ${BDR}$$
  ^\s+Neighbor Count is \d+ \(${PASSIVE}\)$$
  ^\s+${AUTH}(, .*)?$$
